BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-206916@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261028T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261028T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261028T193000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Wealth\, Well Lived
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 5 spots left
 \nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/event
 s/206916\n\n6:00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Discussion\nWhat does it really mean
  to live a wealthy life? In the first of a new\, multi-part series present
 ed with Willow and The Impact Collective we will look beyond what we earn
 \, save\, or invest\, to consider how wealth reflects the choices we make\
 , the opportunities we create\, and the values we carry into our personal 
 and professional lives. Joined by Lacy Garcia\, Founder and CEO of Willow\
 , and Julia Johannsen\, Founder and Executive Director of The Impact Colle
 ctive\, this discussion will explore the intersection of money\, investing
 \, and personal values. Together\, they will begin to decode the systems t
 hat shape our financial lives and consider how greater understanding can l
 ead to more informed\, purposeful decisions. As the series unfolds\, expec
 t to explore conversations such as the wealth gap\, generational planning\
 , roles and representation\, and the ways we can rethink traditional ideas
  of wealth to better align our investments with the lives and\, legacies w
 e want to build.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members 
 only. Complimentary light bites will be served\, with beverages available 
 for purchase throughout the evening. We kindly ask that all cancellations 
 be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206916
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
