BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-206949@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261030T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261030T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261030T190000
SUMMARY:Trials and Truth: A History of Witchcraft
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nStatus: You are Confirmed\
 nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206949\n\n5:30PM Recep
 tion\, 6:00PM Discussion\n\nIn a seasonal ode to witchcraft\, join us for 
 a thought provoking exploration tracing the myths\, origins\, and historie
 s that have shaped its place in a Western European cultural lineage\, a li
 neage that runs through to the Americas and into the present day. Building
  on last year's Trials & Truth\, which examined the Salem Witch Trials\, P
 rofessor Julie Walsh returns to take the conversation beyond local lore\, 
 exploring the European roots of the image of the witch\, its enduring ster
 eotypes\, and the complex relationship between belief\, skepticism\, and t
 he social consequences of believing the worst about your neighbors. The e
 vening will delve into the origin story of the medieval witch\, what this 
 story reveals about power\, fear\, freedom\, and social justice. \n\nJuli
 e Walsh is the Whitehead Associate Professor of Critical Thought\, Associa
 te Professor of Philosophy\, and Director of the Newhouse Center for the H
 umanities at the Wellesley College\; she specializes in early modern philo
 sophy\, theories of freedom\, and the history of witchcraft. She will be i
 n conversation with Liza Oliver\, Associate Professor of Art History and D
 irector of the Pluralism Initiative at Wellesley College\; she specialize
 s in the intersections of art\, colonialism\, and cultural history. Togeth
 er\, they will offer members a fresh perspective on the historical roots a
 nd ongoing social impact of European ideas of witches\, witchcraft\, and e
 vil. \n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Comp
 limentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that 
 all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the even
 t.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206949
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
