BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-208789@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261109T190000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261109T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261109T200000
SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: "Georgia" by Dawn Tripp 
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent U
 RL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208789\n\nBookmark your calend
 ar and settle in for November’s Author Circle Book Club\, Georgia by Daw
 n Tripp—a captivating and richly imagined novel inspired by the extraord
 inary life of iconic American artist Georgia O’Keeffe.\n\nSet against th
 e vibrant art world of early 20th-century New York and the striking landsc
 apes of New Mexico\, Georgia explores the woman behind the art\, tracing h
 er passionate pursuit of independence\, creativity\, and love. Through her
  complex relationship with photographer Alfred Stieglitz and her determina
 tion to forge a path entirely her own\, Tripp paints an intimate portrait 
 of ambition\, identity\, and artistic expression. A beautifully layered st
 ory sure to inspire thoughtful conversation.\n\n*This event is complimenta
 ry and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshmen
 ts will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 
 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208789
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
