SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Art of the City - Why Cultural Philanthropy Matters
  Now
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 68 spots lef
 t\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/2
 09681\n\n2:00PM Reception\, 2:30PM Discussion \n\nTo celebrate Town & Co
 untry’s milestone 180th anniversary\, Editor in Chief Stellene Volandes
  and The ‘Quin Co-Founder Sandy Edgerley will host a timely conversation
  on the vital role cultural philanthropy plays in shaping Boston and its f
 uture.\n\nThe Art of the City - Why Cultural Philanthropy Matters Now brin
 gs together an extraordinary group of leaders from across Boston’s cultu
 ral\, civic\, and philanthropic communities to explore the power of the ar
 ts\, the importance of investing in our cultural institutions\, and the fu
 ture of philanthropy for the next generation.\n\nJoining the conversation 
 along with Stellene and Sandy will be Peggy Fogelman\, Norma Jean Calderwo
 od Director of the Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum and Joseph Henry\, Chie
 f\, Mayor’s Office of Arts and Culture\, City of Boston.\n\nThe discussi
 on will be moderated by Adam Rathe\, Senior Features Director at Town & C
 ountry. A Q&A will follow.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved fo
 r members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served
 . Cancellations made within 24 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\
 , will result in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209681
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
